        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>A welcome return to watch Cambridge brought back a whole lot of memories, nostalgia and contemplation</p><p>On 11 February 1989, Cambridge United beat Hartlepool 6-0. My memories of the game are faint. The internet can’t even tell me who scored – perhaps Laurie Ryan got a couple. I do recall walking past some Hartlepool fans on Coldham’s Common who were peering into a brook. “Looking for a new centre forward?”</p><p>Not a terrible joke from my dad. There was polite laughter at least.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/aug/27/cambridge-united-millwall-carabao-cup-max-rushden-football-supporter\">Continue reading...</a>"
